# Historical survey reference, NOT a SAR reconstruction
# Units: metres; axes x=east y=north z=up; separate simplified volumes
# Not georeferenced, not a watertight engineering model
# https://giza.fas.harvard.edu/pubdocs/141/full/
# 0 m = historical shaft mouth. Rock begins 2.34 m below the mouth; the modern ground datum is not established.
# Simplification: The shaft is represented by its published average square width. Uneven walls are simplified.
# Simplification: The chamber opens south and extends west. The trapezoid uses the reported east/west lengths; its exact angles and junction are simplified from Fig. 13.
# Simplification: The model places the chamber floor at the shaft bottom. Its 5.89 m roof depth is derived from that alignment and the reported 2.16 m height, not independently surveyed here.
# Simplification: Sarcophagus, rubble, wall texture and minor irregularities are omitted. This is an envelope of the excavated spaces, not a watertight engineering survey.
